# ui

Browser tests generated by `sbrs mkdir`.

## Run them

Cargo runs a folder as one test target when it sits directly inside `tests/`
(`tests/<folder>/main.rs`). If this folder is somewhere else, register it in your
crate's `Cargo.toml`:

```toml
[[test]]
name = "ui"
path = "ui/main.rs"
```

Then run it:

```sh
cargo test --test ui
```

The tests need Chrome, and a matching chromedriver unless they are pure CDP;
`sbrs doctor` checks both. Your crate needs only seleniumbase-rs, which re-exports
the rstest attribute, the Tokio runtime and the Gherkin macros the tests use. It is on
GitHub, not on crates.io:

```toml
[dev-dependencies]
seleniumbase-rs = { git = "https://github.com/MustCodeAl/seleniumbase-rs", tag = "v0.6.0", features = ["testing"] }
```

## Settings

The `sb` and `sb_cdp` fixtures read `sbase_config.toml` from the directory you run
`cargo test` in, then apply `SB_*` environment variables, which `sbrs test` sets
from its flags (`--reruns`, `--time-limit`, `--env`, ...). For example,
`SB_HEADLESS=true cargo test --test ui` runs without a window. A failed test
leaves a screenshot, the page source and a report in `latest_logs/`.

## Files

| File | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `main.rs` | The test target; declares the modules below. |
| `my_first_test.rs` | The `sb` fixture: a simple example test; copy it to start your own. |
| `parameterized_test.rs` | `#[case]`: one test body run for each row of a table, each row its own test. |
| `cdp_test.rs` | The `sb_cdp` fixture: pure CDP, with no chromedriver. |
